1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,357
Hi, we're team hack masters, and this is Health Copilot:

2
00:00:04,407 --> 00:00:08,508
an AI-powered personal health copilot for Indian families.

3
00:00:08,558 --> 00:00:17,310
It reads your medical paperwork twice, checks it with code, lets you confirm it, and then explains it in your own language.

4
00:00:18,370 --> 00:00:22,202
Indian patients carry their health history on paper:

5
00:00:22,252 --> 00:00:31,460
handwritten prescriptions, lab printouts and discharge summaries, often mixing English with Hindi, Telugu, Tamil or Kannada.

6
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:37,283
Nobody explains the abnormal values, and records don't move between hospitals.

7
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:42,360
ABDM can carry them, but only as structured FHIR, linked to an ABHA.

8
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:44,797
Let's see it live.

9
00:00:44,847 --> 00:00:50,064
You sign in with your email or your mobile number, and a password.

10
00:00:50,114 --> 00:00:55,810
One account holds a whole family, and it only ever sees its own records.

11
00:00:56,880 --> 00:01:00,002
The dashboard brings every document together:

12
00:01:00,052 --> 00:01:04,442
results that need attention, today's medicines, and conditions.

13
00:01:04,492 --> 00:01:11,420
The High and Low flags are computed in code from the report's own reference range, never by the AI.

14
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:16,665
Now let's upload a photo of a bilingual Telugu prescription.

15
00:01:16,715 --> 00:01:24,782
The pipeline deskews and enhances the page, classifies it, and extracts it with Gemini vision into a strict schema.

16
00:01:24,832 --> 00:01:33,040
Every value is checked in code, and then a different model re-reads the page, focusing on whatever looked suspicious.

17
00:01:33,090 --> 00:01:36,640
An upload can even be deleted before it's reviewed.

18
00:01:37,690 --> 00:01:43,268
While that runs, here's the review screen for a handwritten prescription photo.

19
00:01:43,318 --> 00:01:50,890
The original page sits next to every extracted field, with its confidence, and whether both AI reads agree.

20
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:54,523
This card shows what the verification read changed:

21
00:01:54,573 --> 00:02:00,863
it caught the full brand name, Uprise D3 60K, and removed codes that weren't on the page.

22
00:02:00,913 --> 00:02:04,710
Nothing reaches the record until a person confirms it.

23
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:08,315
Our Telugu prescription is ready.

24
00:02:08,365 --> 00:02:14,630
A quick check, then one tap on Confirm and save, and it joins the family record.

25
00:02:15,690 --> 00:02:22,275
Trends plot every result across the year, with the reference range shaded.

26
00:02:22,325 --> 00:02:25,861
HbA1c came down from 8.1 to 7.6 percent:

27
00:02:25,911 --> 00:02:28,910
better, but still above the range.

28
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:34,978
Every document gets a plain-language explanation, here in Hindi.

29
00:02:35,028 --> 00:02:37,275
The AI writes only the prose.

30
00:02:37,325 --> 00:02:46,540
Each number, flag and schedule is attached from the database, and a safety filter blocks dosing advice and diagnoses.

31
00:02:47,590 --> 00:02:52,974
Ask Copilot answers questions from your own records only, with citations.

32
00:02:53,024 --> 00:02:59,300
Here I'm asking in Telugu about my sugar and cholesterol, and which medicines I take.

33
00:02:59,350 --> 00:03:07,190
The answer comes back in Telugu, with the results and medicines it used, and it can read the answer aloud.

34
00:03:12,790 --> 00:03:14,366
It's ready for ABDM.

35
00:03:14,416 --> 00:03:21,440
Link an ABHA with a one-time password, grant consent, and pull records from a hospital.

36
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:30,710
Every confirmed document becomes an NRCeS-profile FHIR R4 bundle, readable here, with the raw JSON one click away.

37
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:33,609
And it's built for phones:

38
00:03:33,659 --> 00:03:40,694
a bottom tab bar, the account menu in the corner, and it installs to the home screen like an app.

39
00:03:40,744 --> 00:03:43,250
Everything works in five languages.

40
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:45,435
Under the hood:

41
00:03:45,485 --> 00:03:53,337
FastAPI on the back end, React 19 on the front end, and Gemini model chains with automatic fallback.

42
00:03:53,387 --> 00:03:55,708
And it all runs on free tiers:

43
00:03:55,758 --> 00:04:03,610
Render, a private GitHub repository as the datastore, Gmail through Apps Script, and GitHub Actions.

44
00:04:04,670 --> 00:04:08,046
We measured accuracy instead of claiming it.

45
00:04:08,096 --> 00:04:19,570
On ten test documents, including handwriting, phone photos and four Indian scripts, the pipeline with verification got all 477 checked fields right.

46
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:23,230
AI reads and explains.

47
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:24,670
Code checks.

48
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:26,110
You confirm.

49
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:31,630
Your record, in your language, ready for ABDM.

50
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:32,830
Thank you!
